  "body": "Found during #3021.\n\n## What happens\nPR for #3021 adds closing wall and island rings to the plain 2D Zigzag pocket (`pocket_over_with_relief` in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/pocket.rs`). Two other pass plans still cut Zigzag rows with no closing ring:\n\n- `pocket_avoid` (2D pocket with \"Do not touch\"), `crates/motion/src/machining2d/pocket_avoid.rs`: each level calls `plan_passes(..., strategy)`, and Zigzag gives rows only.\n- The 3D pocket levels that call `plan_passes` with Zigzag or Auto.\n\nThe rows touch a wall or an island only at their ends. A cusp stays between each two ends over the full depth (about 0.17 mm on a straight wall with a 6 mm tool and a 2 mm stepover, more on a rounded corner).\n\n## Expected\nWith stock to leave 0, the Zigzag rows of these plans close with one ring on each boundary loop, as the plain 2D pocket does after #3021. Use `pocket_zigzag::rest_passes` (rows 0.01 mm inside, lattice row points, then the rings).\n\n## Related observation\nA 30 x 30 pocket with a 10 x 10 island, an 8 mm tool, a 3 mm stepover and a helix entry gives crossing feed pairs between two helix entries of different passes. The cutter-center band is only 2 mm wide there. The post check blocks the program. This is on upstream/main before #3021 too. The pin `blended_zigzag_turns_do_not_cross_the_closing_rings` uses a plunge entry for this reason.\n\n## Done means\nA pin like `crates/motion/tests/pocket_wall_finish.rs` for `pocket_avoid` (and for a 3D pocket level) fails before the change and passes after it. The crossing check stays clean.\n",
